                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "TL;DR:\n------------------------------------------------------\nI liked the game and its systems, but there is little to no replay value after your initial play, which will become plagued with lag the longer your playthrough runs.\n------------------------------------------------------\n\nPlanet Stronghold is an interesting mixed bag, initially I thought it was better than Loren: The Amazon Princess, and in regards to combat/leveling I think it is a more compelling system... however things fall apart when you realize there is no visual novel mode after beating the game.\n\nVisual Novel mode made it easy to see other paths without having to entirely replay through the game, Planet Stronghold however has never received that mode/option which makes seeing other paths rather painful.\n\nIf the combat is better why is it painful? Well you see every archetype for combat in one run, so there's nothing new by changing yours, second if you are like me and do EVERY battle than there is nothing more to experience with the combat, meaning you are just going through the exact same content again.\n\nIf this game didn't have so many performance issues due to its aged engine and had visual novel mode, I would give it a glowing recommendation. As is though while I would recommend it to Winter Wolves fans, for new comers try one of their other games first.",
